# Code owners must approve a change to anything that runs, with someone's
# credentials, on a maintainer's or contributor's machine or in CI. A pull
# request from a fork can change any of these files, so each is listed.
# Enforced only while the branch ruleset for main requires code-owner review.
#
# The owner is a team, not people: any member can approve, and a handle that is
# misspelt or that has left cannot silently make every review impossible. The
# team needs Write access to this repository (Settings > Collaborators and
# teams); GitHub ignores an owner without it and reports a CODEOWNERS error.

# AI agent configuration. Skills, rules and instruction files are read by
# review and coding agents as trusted context (a PR that edits them can embed
# instructions such as "ignore all vulnerabilities"), and some of them run
# code: .claude/settings.json holds shell hooks and .opencode/plugins/ holds a
# JavaScript plugin, both run when a maintainer opens the branch in the agent.
# .github/skills, .claude/skills and .opencode/skills are only symlinks to
# .agents/skills, so the real directory has to be named, not the links; the
# links themselves are listed without a trailing slash, so that pointing one
# somewhere else needs approval too. skills-lock.json pins the external skills.
/.agents/ @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.claude/ @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.opencode/ @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.github/skills @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/AGENTS.md @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/CLAUDE.md @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.github/copilot-instructions.md @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.coderabbit.yaml @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/skills-lock.json @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders

# Git hooks: .githooks/pre-commit runs on every commit of anyone who sets
# core.hooksPath to it.
/.githooks/ @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders

# CI and everything CI executes. The workflow runs `just` recipes, the shell
# scripts and Dockerfiles under tests/ and docker/, and builds the crate
# (build scripts and dependencies come from Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock). Today
# CI has no secrets; the day a release workflow gets some, these are the files
# that would run next to them.
/.github/workflows/ @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.github/CODEOWNERS @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.github/dependabot.yml @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/.yamllint.yaml @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
# .gitattributes can mark a file so that GitHub hides its diff in a review.
/.gitattributes @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/justfile @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/tests/ @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/docker/ @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/Cargo.toml @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
/Cargo.lock @gyrforge/gyrseek-builders
